Inserting before the head (Prepend)

When you insert a node at the front, you already have direct access to the head pointer.
You don't need to search through the list, making this operation exceptionally fast.

void insertAtHead(Node*& head, int data) {
    Node* newNode = new Node(data);

    //Edge case: The list is currently empty 
    if (head == nullptr) {
        head = newNode;
        return;
    }

    //Step 1: Connect the new node to the current head 
    newNode->next = head;

    //Step 2: Connect the current head back to new node 
    head->prev = newNode;

    //Step 3: Shift the head pointer to the new first node 
    head = newNode;
}

Because you are modifying the front of list, you only need to reroute the next pointer of 
your new node and the prev pointer of the old head. You never have to touch the rest of the list.

